  "id": "three-way-analysis-of-variance",
  "term": "three-way analysis of variance",
  "definition": "Three-way analysis of variance is a statistical method used to test how three different factors, and their interactions, are related to variation in an outcome. In this study, it was used to examine how shade, geographical origin, and genotype were linked to differences in plant traits.",
